# @NAME@ — PC (SDL2)

The same firmware the consoles run, as a SDL2 window: the emulation, the
option menu (hold Escape), the save states and the SD card are those of the
shared frontend. The save states need no card: the slots are a plain file in
the working directory (the state file's name, e.g. `GAME.STA`), created on
the first save. The card is the file `sd.img` in the working directory —
`dd if=/dev/zero of=sd.img bs=1M count=8 && mkfs.fat -F 16 sd.img` makes one
(put the game's `.GB`/`.SAV` files on it as compile.sh does for the META).
Without it the game still runs; states work, the cartridge's battery saves
and streamed cartridges need the image.

- Window: the source console's native resolution, scaled to the window.
- Pad: arrows or gamepad D-pad/left stick, X = A, Z = B, Return or gamepad Start = Menu,
  Escape/Backspace or gamepad Back = Home (hold: options). Generic joysticks use
  their axes/hat and buttons 0–4. Controllers can be connected while running.
- Display: unfiltered pixels by default; F8 cycles pixel, DMG, LCD RGB,
  scanlines, grid and back to none. F10 changes scaling; F11 toggles fullscreen.

Build and run:

```
cmake -B build . && cmake --build build && ./build/@NAME@
```

`M0_FRAMES=<n>` exits after n frames (dumping the last one to `M0_PPM=path`),
which is what the automated test runs.
